        "recap": "山腹里有人断绳封井。沈砚与罗清带着残账逃出，赶往东渡口找周伯。",
        "cn": [
          "河风刺骨，艄公一见沈砚的山门衣袍，便要退还船钱。他不信门中的口头[[assurance|保证]]，怕这趟船最终被扣走。沈砚脱下外袍，罗清报出医馆的名字，写下赔船的[[pledge|承诺]]，艄公才解开系缆。小船被风推向芦苇，沈砚接过磨掉漆皮的[[oar|船桨]]。对岸没灯，他只能[[rely|依靠]]水撞桥墩的声音辨路。桨下忽然碰到暗石，他按住船边，让罗清坐稳，自己俯身把船慢慢撑过去。",
          "旧庙门口，周伯正拆一张草席，听见脚步便举起竹刀。直到银扣在灯下露出来，他才认出这是沈母留下的[[relic|遗物]]。银扣传给历任守户，铜钥匙留在守渠人手里，本就不该由一家握全。沈砚请他[[confess|坦白]]为何失踪，老人反问：你找田，还是找水？沈砚答两样都找，将[[genuine|真实的]]残账摆上石案。周伯放下刀，从席缝取出记载各年水税的[[chronicle|记录]]，纸边虽潮，字却没有散。",
          "十二年前大旱，沈母按人口与田亩算出各家[[quota|配额]]，牵头立下共用水源的[[treaty|协议]]。那不是山门赐水，而是山上山下各自让出一部分。后来石台建成，她与周伯分持银扣、铜匙，相互[[supervise|监督]]。母亲去世后，韩长老将旧约斥为过时的[[custom|习俗]]，收回公开账册。周伯不肯交匙，便被赶下山，连孙女的药也断了。他说到这里，把账末一页按回袖中。沈砚看见纸上的血迹，没急着伸手。",
          "罗清替周伯换绷带，发现背上的伤是受过[[lash|鞭打]]，并非管事声称的跌倒。她敷上随身的[[remedy|伤药]]，说感染还得回医馆处理，不能靠这一包粉末保证无事。周伯问沈砚，会不会拿自己换回药田？沈砚说先要[[verify|核实]]两本账的差别，再请他当众讲明。话未说完，窗纸上钉进一支箭。艄公拉开后门，罗清答应做老人的[[escort|护送者]]；沈砚举起石案边的木板，挡着他们冲进杂木林。",
          "追赶的号角从河边传来，几人伏在半山石亭歇气。周伯把铜匙交给沈砚，却仍将末页[[conceal|藏住]]。他只说，上面记着十二年前死去的人。前方石路已有火把，罗清在泥地划出通往医馆的[[alternative|另一条路线]]。母亲的名字竟与死亡相连，沈砚心底生出一阵[[dread|恐惧]]。他想追问，又看见老人衣背渗血，便收紧装账的布包。先把活人送到安全处，这是他此刻能守住的[[vow|誓言]]，旧事等天亮再问。"
        ],
        "en": [
          "The river wind cut through them. Seeing Shen's mountain robe, the boatman offered their fare back. He distrusted the sect's verbal [[assurance|assurance]] and feared his boat would be seized. Shen removed the robe. Luo gave the clinic's name and wrote a [[pledge|pledge]] to pay for the boat if necessary. Only then did the boatman untie it. Wind pushed them toward the reeds, and Shen took the worn [[oar|oar]]. With no light on the opposite bank, he had to [[rely|rely]] on the sound of water striking the bridge supports. The oar touched a hidden rock. He steadied the boat, told Luo to sit firmly, and leaned forward to push them slowly clear.",
          "At the old temple, Zhou was pulling a mat apart. He raised a bamboo knife at their footsteps, then recognized the silver clasp as a [[relic|relic]] left by Shen's mother. It passed between successive field keepers, while the channel keeper held the copper key. No household was meant to have both. Shen asked him to [[confess|confess]] why he had disappeared. Zhou asked whether he wanted his field or the water. Both, Shen answered, laying the [[genuine|genuine]] ledger fragment on the stone table. Zhou lowered the knife and drew a [[chronicle|chronicle]] of annual water taxes from the mat's seam. The edges were damp, but the writing remained clear.",
          "During a drought twelve years earlier, Shen's mother had calculated each household's [[quota|quota]] from its people and fields. She helped establish a [[treaty|treaty]] for sharing the spring. The mountain had not bestowed the water; both sides had surrendered part of their claims. When the platform was built, she and Zhou kept the clasp and copper key separately so they could [[supervise|supervise]] each other. After her death, Han dismissed the agreement as an obsolete [[custom|custom]] and removed the public ledger. Zhou refused to surrender his key and was expelled. Even his granddaughter's medicine was stopped. He pushed the final page into his sleeve. Shen saw blood on it but did not reach for it.",
          "Changing Zhou's bandage, Luo found wounds from a [[lash|lash]], rather than the fall the steward had described. She applied a [[remedy|remedy]] from her bag but said the infection needed treatment at the clinic. One packet of powder could not guarantee his safety. Zhou asked whether Shen would exchange him for his field. Shen said he first needed to [[verify|verify]] the difference between the ledgers, then ask Zhou to explain it publicly. Before he finished, an arrow struck the window paper. The boatman opened the rear door. Luo agreed to be Zhou's [[escort|escort]], and Shen raised a board from beside the table to shield their escape into the trees.",
          "A pursuing horn sounded from the river. They rested low in a hillside pavilion. Zhou handed over the copper key but continued to [[conceal|conceal]] the final page. He said only that it named people who had died twelve years earlier. Torches already lined the road ahead. Luo drew an [[alternative|alternative]] route to her clinic in the mud. Learning that his mother's name might be linked to deaths filled Shen with [[dread|dread]]. He wanted to question Zhou, then saw blood soaking through the old man's back. He tightened the cloth around the ledger. His present [[vow|vow]] was to get the living to safety. The past could wait until morning."
        ]
