          "[[quarterly|Quarterly]] tool photographs showed B-17 boxes [[recur|recur]] in one corner. I would not [[generalize|generalize]] all cargo from them. Beside a [[dwarf|dwarf]] palm, however, a missing patch of [[grease|grease]] matched repeatedly. The director continued to [[allege|allege]] front-door delivery, saying visitors respected the tower like a [[pilgrim|pilgrim]]. Cheng did not let this [[trigger|trigger]] argument. She sought to [[assimilate|assimilate]] times and [[segregate|segregate]] public catalogue entries from experimental stock. Chen mapped the route, allowing the worker to speak without shouting.",
          "We gained permission to examine storage records, but found only new labels. The stamp confirmed sample reception, not original batches. Tool photographs revealed a museum paper bag whose transfer date preceded the claimed arrival by three months. The director called it a souvenir. Why did its box reappear among sample returns? Flags tightened outside; ferry warnings predicted cancellation. We took rooms and arranged to investigate the museum bag tomorrow, without allowing approaching weather to determine our answer first."
