          "She would not [[bury|bury]] errors and bought [[butter|butter]] bread beside a closed [[cafe|cafe]]. A [[calculus|calculus]] club poster showed ordinary school life continuing beyond altered transfers. A [[calibration|calibration]] date on waste printing material distinguished editions; a guard thought it merely [[camp|camp]] paper. Cheng photographed both sides. Wu identified her signed original, six months earlier than island relabelling. Her signature had been borrowed for a batch she had never seen. The distortion became something precise, not a general printing mistake.",
